// Navigation: the pages of an application and the navigators that hold them.
//
// A window is a surface -- something on screen the user can close -- and a
// page is a destination: an `href`, a title, and the parameters a route hands
// it. `stack` holds pages one on top of another, `go` pushes and `back` pops,
// and which page is showing is state the stack keeps, read through its handle:
//
//	ui.window(title="Docs - {pages.current.title}") {
//	    nav.link(to=about, text="About")
//	    nav.stack #pages {
//	        nav.page #home(href="/") { … }
//	        nav.page #about(href="/about", title="About") { … }
//	    }
//	}
//
// Where that state lives is each target's: the URL on html, the back stack the
// system button pops on android, a field of the Model on a desktop or a
// terminal. A page is named by its `#id`, so a misspelled destination is an
// unresolved name rather than a dead link.
